# The cloudflare profile: hosting on Cloudflare Workers for an app on the vite-react-tanstack
# profile. One Worker serves the built client as static assets and answers /api/* with a
# Hono app. Opt in with `cloudflare` in the project's .template-profiles, after
# vite-react-tanstack. Same syntax as .template/manifest, but every path is read from
# .template/profiles/cloudflare/ rather than from the template's root.
#
# Everything it manages is in .devtools/host/, which the vite-react-tanstack profile's
# shared configs load when it exists: its Vite plugin, its Vitest project, its ESLint rules
# and its make targets. Nothing in the project's own config files names the host, so a
# project lists one hosting profile at a time, and moving to another is a swap of names in
# .template-profiles and a sync.
#
# Per project, and not listed: wrangler.jsonc, .dev.vars.example, everything under worker/,
# and the job in release.yml that deploys a release (deploy.yml shows it). `node
# .devtools/scripts/gen.mjs host` writes a first version of the files and installs the
# packages; `gen.mjs app` does the same when the profile is there first.

file  .devtools/host/host.mk
file  .devtools/host/vite.ts
file  .devtools/host/vitest.ts
file  .devtools/host/eslint.js
file  .devtools/host/scaffold.mjs
file  .github/workflows/deploy.yml

block .gitignore           cloudflare
block pnpm-workspace.yaml  cloudflare
block AGENTS.md            cloudflare
